+------------------------------------------------------------
-- @DESC: grow a list with <+ inside a for loop (E6)
------------------------------------------------------------+
rule main:
  new sq := ();
  for i ∈ (1..5) do
    let sq <+ i * i;
  done;
  expect sq = (1,4,9,16,25);
  expect sq[3] = 9;
return;
+------------------------------------------------------------
spec/10 §3.2 + spec/02 §3.4: a `for` loop seeds a fresh empty
list and `<+` appends each iteration's computed value, proving
loop-local mutation persists on the enclosing collection.
------------------------------------------------------------+
